            "value": "A glycopeptide produced by the bacterium <em>Streptomyces verticillus</em>. The term, 'bleomycin' refers to a family of structurally related compounds. When used as an anti-cancer agent, the chemotherapeutical forms are primarily bleomycin A<small><sub>2</sub></small> and B<small><sub>2</sub></small>."
