            "stanza": "CHEBI:59062",
            "subject": "CHEBI:59062",
            "value": "Polymyxins are antibiotics with a general structure consisting of a cyclic peptide with a long hydrophobic tail. They disrupt the structure of the bacterial cell membrane by interacting with its phospholipids. Polymyxins are produced by the Gram-positive bacterium <em>Bacillus polymyxa</em> and are selectively toxic for Gram-negative bacteria."
