      "reason": "Preserve the complete original negative decision; current target/alias/source changes do not resolve its full scientific scope. Current named assertion MIM:0002196 (Riboflavin) skos:exactMatch CHEBI:17015 (riboflavin) was assessed against its actual owner and captured CHEBI declaration. The own-identifier or exact named-concept relation retains its substance/class boundary, salt, hydration and stereochemical qualifications. The actual published alias field is '1-deoxy-1-(7,8-dimethyl-2,4-dioxo-3,4-dihydrobenzo[g]pteridin-10(2H)-yl)-D-ribitol|1-deoxy-1-(7,8-dimethyl-2,4-dioxo-3,4-dihydrobenzo[g]pteridin-10(2H)-yl)pentitol|5-deoxy-5-(7,8-dimethyl-2,4-dioxo-3,4-dihydrobenzo[g]pteridin-10(2H)-yl)-D-ribitol|6,7-dimethyl-9-D-ribitylisoalloxazine|7,8-dimethyl-10-(D-ribo-2,3,4,5-tetrahydroxypentyl)benzo[g]pteridine-2,4(3H,10H)-dione|7,8-dimethyl-10-(D-ribo-2,3,4,5-tetrahydroxypentyl)isoalloxazine|7,8-dimethyl-10-[(2S,3S,4R)-2,3,4,5-tetrahydroxypentyl]benzo[g]pteridine-2,4(3H,10H)-dione|7,8-dimethyl-10-ribitylisoalloxazine|Aqua-Flave|Beflavin|Beflavine|Bisulase|Dermadram|E101|Fiboflavin|Flavaxin|Flavin Bb|Flaxain|Hyflavin|Riboflavine|Riboflavine (B2)|Riboflavin (Vitamine B2)|Riboflavin (Vitamin B2)|Riboflavin (0.2 mg/ml)|Riboflavin (see below)|Riboflavin (0.05 μg/mL)|CAS:83-88-5'; rejected labels and competing-owner tokens remain suppressed, not silently approved.  Every source/comment token is assessed as attributed history, not new evidence acquisition. Latest-event mapping_date and deterministic confidence do not grant science; removed validation stamps are preserved in beforeimages. No role, occurrence, source-binding, quantity, component, owner-merge, subclass or release approval follows.",
