      "reason": "Preserve the complete original negative decision; current target/alias/source changes do not resolve its full scientific scope. Current named assertion MIM:0002493 (Thiamine pyrophosphate) skos:exactMatch CHEBI:9532 (thiamine(1+) diphosphate) was assessed against its actual owner and captured CHEBI declaration. The own-identifier or exact named-concept relation retains its substance/class boundary, salt, hydration and stereochemical qualifications. The actual published alias field is \"3-[(4-amino-2-methylpyrimidin-5-yl)methyl]-5-(2-diphosphoethyl)-4-methyl-1,3-thiazolium chloride|3-[(4-amino-2-methylpyrimidin-5-yl)methyl]-5-(2-{[hydroxy(phosphonooxy)phosphoryl]oxy}ethyl)-4-methyl-1,3-thiazol-3-ium chloride|3-[(4-amino-2-methylpyrimidin-5-yl)methyl]-5-[2-(diphosphooxy)ethyl]-4-methyl-1,3-thiazol-3-ium chloride|Coenzymate|Thiazolium, 3-((4-amino-2-methyl-5-pyrimidinyl)methyl)-4-methyl-5-(4,6,6-trihydroxy-3,5-dioxa-4,6-diphosphahex-1-yl)-, chloride, P,P'-dioxide|cocarboxilasa|cocarboxylase|cocarboxylase chloride|cocarboxylasum|thiamine diphosphate chloride|thiamine diphosphoric acid ester chloride|thiamine(1+) diphosphate chloride|thiaminium diphosphoric acid ester chloride|thiaminium pyrophosphate chloride|thiaminium pyrophosphoric acid ester chloride|vitamin B1 pyrophosphate chloride|Co Carboxylase|thiamine pyrophosphate chloride|TPP|Co-carboxylase|CAS:136-09-4\"; rejected labels and competing-owner tokens remain suppressed, not silently approved.  Every source/comment token is assessed as attributed history, not new evidence acquisition. Latest-event mapping_date and deterministic confidence do not grant science; removed validation stamps are preserved in beforeimages. No role, occurrence, source-binding, quantity, component, owner-merge, subclass or release approval follows.",
